      "body": "## Motivation\n\nMiniMax H3's full-loop denoising stage rejects out-of-tree platforms because its platform allowlist only includes CUDA, HIP, CPU, MPS, NPU, and XPU.\n\nThis prevents out-of-tree backends from reaching the denoising loop, even when they provide the required device APIs and operators.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Accept `current_platform.is_out_of_tree()` in the full-loop denoising platform check.\n- Update the error message to include out-of-tree platforms.\n\nThis change removes the platform gate for out-of-tree backends. Each backend remains responsible for implementing the required operations.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39189359315](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39189359315)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39189359317](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39189359317)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39189359370](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39189359370)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
